# Trivy ignore file for Hugo static site
# This file contains vulnerability IDs that can be safely ignored for a static website

# Hugo-specific ignores
# These are typically not applicable to static sites

# Example ignores (uncomment and modify as needed):
# CVE-2023-XXXX  # Ignore specific CVE that doesn't apply to static sites
# GHSA-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX  # Ignore GitHub Security Advisory

# Node.js development dependencies that don't affect production
# (Uncomment if you have a package.json with dev dependencies)
# npm:**/node_modules/**/test/**
# npm:**/node_modules/**/tests/**
# npm:**/node_modules/**/*.test.js
# npm:**/node_modules/**/*.spec.js

# Documentation and example files
**/example/**
**/examples/**
**/test/**
**/tests/**
**/*.test.*
**/*.spec.*
**/README.md
**/CHANGELOG.md
**/LICENSE*

# Ignore secrets scanning for common false positives
generic-api-key:tests/**
generic-api-key:examples/**
aws-access-key-id:tests/**
aws-secret-access-key:tests/**
